#!/usr/bin/env ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

# Differential harness for the HTTP API: `bin/tasks-api` and `go/cmd/tasks-api`
# started against IDENTICAL copies of one fixture, driven with the same
# requests, and compared byte for byte.
#
# This is the tool the Wave 3 API packet was judged by, and it exists because
# every bug that mattered in Waves 1 and 2 was found by running the two
# implementations against each other, never by reading code.
#
# Usage:
#
#   porting/api-differential            # all three phases
#   porting/api-differential reads      # one phase
#
# Phases:
#
#   reads      every GET, against an untouched store. Compared with only the
#              request id normalized, because nothing else may differ.
#   transport  the refusals — media type, body limit, host, origin, precondition.
#   writes     a stateful create/patch sequence, plus the resulting store bytes.
#              Normalized for minted ids, revision digests and today's date,
#              because two independent servers legitimately differ in all three
#              (see porting/intentional-differences.md,
#              `go-api-honours-the-determinism-pins`).
#
# Exit status is 0 when every comparison in the requested phases agrees EXCEPT
# the routes recorded as intentionally refused; any other divergence is a defect.

